  "why": "The paper empirically demonstrates that DRFuzz finds many regression faults in models that underwent adversarial training (a common safeguard): the authors include adversarial training (ADV:BIM and ADV:CW) as explicit regression scenarios and report large numbers of regression-fault-triggering inputs detected by DRFuzz in those scenarios. However, DRFuzz was not specifically designed to target safeguards: its failure oracle is the general prediction-difference oracle (cM1[x]=y and cM2[x]≠y) and its search/mutation strategies (MCMC-guided mutation selection, GAN-based fidelity filtering, seed maintenance) are general-purpose for regression fuzzing rather than encoding bypass conditions or using feedback from defenses. Thus the paper demonstrates successful bypasses of an instantiated safeguard (adversarial training) without having been explicitly designed to discover safeguard bypasses.",
